---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Precision, without complication"
  description="About ENG Drawing Viewer, the free offline drawing workspace by ca-works, and its licensing."
>
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="section-tag">ABOUT & LEGAL</div>
      <h1>
        Precision, without
        <br />
        <span>complication.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        ENG Drawing Viewer is an independent engineering drawing application by
        ca-works, designed to make reviewing and sharing technical information
        feel simple.
      </p>
    </header>
    <article class="page-content prose">
      <h2>Built around the drawing</h2>
      <p>
        Browse a project, see the smallest detail, add a clear review and take
        it into your next presentation. When a drawing needs more, edit the PDF,
        retouch a photo or trace a part into vectors. The application brings
        those everyday tasks together in a local desktop workspace for Mac,
        Windows and Linux.
      </p>
      <h2>Free software</h2>
      <p>
        ENG Drawing Viewer is free software under the{' '}
        <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html">
          GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 or later
        </a>
        . Its complete source code, build instructions and the source of every
        copyleft library it includes are published with each release in the{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/ca-works/eng-drawing-viewer">GitHub repository</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        Free software is provided without warranty, to the extent permitted by
        applicable law. Verify drawing dimensions and export results before
        relying on them for engineering or manufacturing decisions.
      </p>
      <h2>Third-party components</h2>
      <p>
        The desktop application uses PySide6/Qt, PyMuPDF/MuPDF, Python, Pillow,
        NumPy, OpenCV, ONNX Runtime, ezdxf, libheif, python-pptx, python-docx
        and XlsxWriter, among other components. Help › About in the app lists
        every bundled component with its licence text, and each release
        attaches the unmodified source of the copyleft libraries inside it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This website uses Astro, Tailwind CSS and three.js (MIT), GSAP (its Standard No
        Charge licence), Inter and JetBrains Mono (SIL Open Font License). Font
        files are self-hosted. Third-party notices and font licences are
        included with the website source.
      </p>
      <h2>Names and marks</h2>
      <p>
        ENG Drawing Viewer’s name and original blue application icon belong to
        its independent creator. Apple, macOS, iPhone, Microsoft, Windows,
        PowerPoint, LibreOffice and Linux are names or marks of their respective
        owners (Linux® is the registered trademark of Linus Torvalds). This project is not affiliated with those organizations.
      </p>
      <h2>Publisher</h2>
      <p>
        © 2026 ca-works.{' '}
        <a href={site.repo}>Project website source on GitHub ↗</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        For product questions, use the project’s{' '}
        <a href={`${site.repo}/issues`}>support issues</a>. Do not include
        confidential documents or personal information.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
